 "section_summary": "This section (pages 174–225) contains a portion of the postwar 'Roster of Japanese Educational Institutions' for Ishikawa Prefecture. It presents detailed statistical tables cataloging prefectural, municipal, town, village, and private educational facilities, including middle schools, girls' high schools, special schools, vocational and industrial schools, youth schools, elementary schools, and kindergartens. Each school entry records the institutional name, location, founding date, and comparative student enrollment and faculty numbers (categorized by sex and part-time status) for April 30, 1946, and November 30, 1946.",
