   "summary": "This section of the roster catalogs educational institutions across Ishikawa Prefecture, covering prefectural, municipal, town and village, and private schools. It encompasses secondary schools, special schools for the blind and deaf-mute, vocational and industrial schools, youth schools, elementary schools, and kindergartens. Each entry details the school's administrative classification, location, date of founding, and gender-disaggregated statistics for student enrollment and teaching staff as of April 30, 1946, and November 30, 1946.",
